  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:13:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Though I speak with the tongues of men and of angels, and have not charity, I am become as sounding brass, or a tinkling cymbal.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 13:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:13:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:13:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "And though I have the gift of prophecy, and understand all mysteries, and all knowledge; and though I have all faith, so that I could remove mountains, and have not charity, I am nothing.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 13:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:13:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:13:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "And though I bestow all my goods to feed the poor, and though I give my body to be burned, and have not charity, it profiteth me nothing.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 13:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:13:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:13:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "Charity suffereth long, and is kind; charity envieth not; charity vaunteth not itself, is not puffed up,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 13:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:13:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:13:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "Doth not behave itself unseemly, seeketh not her own, is not easily provoked, thinketh no evil;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 13:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:13:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:13:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "Rejoiceth not in iniquity, but rejoiceth in the truth;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 13:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:13:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:13:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "Beareth all things, believeth all things, hopeth all things, endureth all things.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 13:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:13:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:13:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "Charity never faileth: but whether there be prophecies, they shall fail; whether there be tongues, they shall cease; whether there be knowledge, it shall vanish away.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 13:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:13:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:13:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "For we know in part, and we prophesy in part.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 13:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:13:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:13:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "But when that which is perfect is come, then that which is in part shall be done away.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 13:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:13:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:13:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "When I was a child, I spake as a child, I understood as a child, I thought as a child: but when I became a man, I put away childish things.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 13:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:13:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:13:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "For now we see through a glass, darkly; but then face to face: now I know in part; but then shall I know even as also I am known.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 13:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:13:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:13:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "And now abideth faith, hope, charity, these three; but the greatest of these is charity.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 13:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:13:13"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
